  "scope": "For every r>=2 the connected family has p_v=2r and p_u>=r(r+1), giving vp/vp^->=(r+1)/2. For k=2^h, h>=2, the connected bipartite subcubic family has p_v=2k and p_u>=(k-1)(k-2)/2+k, giving vp/vp^->=(k^2-k+2)/(4k). This refutes the boundedness question [Problem 4, DOI 10.7151/dmgt.2491](https://doi.org/10.7151/dmgt.2491), [author version](https://oro.open.ac.uk/87516/8/87516_EA.pdf), preprint arXiv:2209.00359v2 Problem 2.4.",
